<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulrich Rösch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1426–<a href="/years/1491">1491</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulrich Rösch was abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a> from 1463 until his death in 1491, after serving as its administrator from 1457. A baker's son, he restored the abbey's finances, bought the County of Toggenburg in 1468 and built a strong territorial state in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. His plan to move the abbey to Rorschach led the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a> and the Appenzellers to destroy the new building in 1489.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulrich-rosch.jpg" alt="Ulrich Rösch" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uncredited, 15th or 16th century. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abt_Ulrich_R%C3%B6sch_(1463-1491).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
